# Design stack

The full reference is `/ai/design-stack/README.md` (from Windows: `\\wsl.localhost\Ubuntu\ai\design-stack\README.md`). 
This skill is the short version.

## Principle

The design decisions are yours whenever Mo asks you for the work. Skills are instruments: they supply vocabulary, 
references and checks. Make every decision deliberately, using skill defaults, templates and style databases as input 
to your own call. `DESIGN.md` and `PRODUCT.md` in the project are the contract; read them before touching UI and keep 
them true.

Governance (`/ai/governance/README.md`) is simple: whichever AI Mo asks owns the task, visual decisions included. On 
shared surfaces, read the project's notes and `KEEP` list and build on them.

## Tool map

| Moment | Use |
|---|---|
| Set up or refresh the contract | `impeccable` ├óÔÇáÔÇÖ `init` (PRODUCT.md), `document` (DESIGN.md, Google format); 
lint with `npx @google/design.md lint DESIGN.md` |
| Explore directions (new surface or redesign, when asked) | `stitch-design` skills (`generate-design`, 
`code-to-design`, `extract-design-md`) once the Stitch MCP is enabled; otherwise `impeccable shape` / `impeccable 
live` |
